["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Music Number (ISMN)](https://ismn-international.org/ismn/the-ismn/) is a unique numeric identifier for printed music (notated music) standardized by [ISO 10957](https://www.iso.org/standard/83122.html). It consists of either 10 characters (starting with the letter \"M\" for assignments prior to January 1, 2008) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISMN is composed of four parts: the GS1 prefix `979-0`, a registrant element, an item element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9790006538424`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N3d4931c0e4d741e1aa081fb57b68898b", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#class", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/FileKindType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/DefinedProcess", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#nodeKind", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#IRI", "globalId", "", ""]
["_:N0c6a6e5ab83c42b68d29307ba429f2d2", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#class", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/Element", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/gln", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Global Location Number (GLN)](https://www.gs1.org/standards/id-keys/gln) is a 13-digit number, assigned by GS1, that uniquely identifies a legal entity (e.g., a company or customer), a function within a legal entity, a physical location (e.g., a warehouse or a specific shelf in a store), or a digital location (e.g., an Electronic Data Interchange (EDI) gateway).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/HashAlgorithm/blake2b256", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "blake2b256", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string", "", ""]
